Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:43:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] fix(reconciler): release a deleted resource's allocation
 by uid

The Terminating path looked the allocation up by "{kind}/{name}". That
key ignores the namespace, so deleting a service could release the
allocation of a same-name service in another namespace, and it never
matched the allocations the registry now records per resource uid.

Release the active allocation owned by the resource's uid within its
tenant via release_active_allocation; its devices are freed with it.
When the resource has already been deleted, or the name was re-created
under a new uid before this pass, release only the old uid's allocation
and finish, instead of stripping the finalizer from and deleting the
new resource.
